  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "While it is no problem to store a 2 GB file in Fedora it seems to be impossible to get that file back from Fedora.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After digging into the source code I found a check for a maximum file size in",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "fedora.server.storage.lowlevel.GenericFileSystem line 170:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "if (lFileLength > Integer.MAX_VALUE) {",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "throw new LowlevelStorageException(true, \"file \" + getPath(file) + \"too large for reading\");",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "}",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "What is the reason behind that check? Could the check be removed?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In my tests I could successfully retrieve a 2 GB file after commenting out the above code.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Thanks for your help!",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Best regards,",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "AndrÃ©",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
