  "description": "<p>While it is no problem to store a 2 GB file in Fedora it seems to be impossible to get that file back from Fedora.</p>\n\n<p>After digging into the source code I found a check for a maximum file size in</p>\n\n<p>fedora.server.storage.lowlevel.GenericFileSystem line 170:</p>\n\n<p>if (lFileLength &gt; Integer.MAX_VALUE) {<br/>\n    throw new LowlevelStorageException(true, \"file \" + getPath(file) + \"too large for reading\");<br/>\n}</p>\n\n<p>What is the reason behind that check? Could the check be removed?</p>\n\n<p>In my tests I could successfully retrieve a 2 GB file after commenting out the above code.</p>\n\n<p>Thanks for your help!</p>\n\n<p>Best regards,</p>\n\n<p>AndrÃ©</p>",
